WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.838 --> 00:00:04.879
The summer shutdown is ending, and line 3 stands in hall B.

2
00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:07.358
The line is in place.

3
00:00:08.083 --> 00:00:10.451
Now the new way of working has to last.

4
00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:15.117
We follow this one project through the four topics of the module.

5
00:00:15.803 --> 00:00:18.264
The details come later, in the lessons.

6
00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:22.641
The first topic is Standardised work and training.

7
00:00:23.373 --> 00:00:25.173
Will everyone work the same way?

8
00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:28.550
The operators get a work instruction.

9
00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:32.869
One A4 page per task, with photos of the real line.

10
00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:38.921
Someone who was not involved tries the instruction out while the team lead watches.

11
00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:42.540
Where they hesitate, the instruction is unclear.

12
00:00:43.547 --> 00:00:47.587
Just before the start the team lead trains every shift on the floor.

13
00:00:48.315 --> 00:00:51.717
The night shift too, because projects often forget it.

14
00:00:52.746 --> 00:00:55.359
For standardised work and training we often

15
00:00:55.405 --> 00:00:58.342
use a skills matrix and a training timetable.

16
00:00:59.611 --> 00:01:02.049
The second topic is Adoption and handover.

17
00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:03.978
Is it really used?

18
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.374
That is called adoption.

19
00:01:07.074 --> 00:01:10.986
People really use the new way, even when nobody is watching.

20
00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:13.903
That works when they helped shape it,

21
00:01:14.077 --> 00:01:17.293
their team lead asks about it and the old way is gone.

22
00:01:18.351 --> 00:01:20.708
Then the project hands over to the line.

23
00:01:21.419 --> 00:01:23.706
The team lead becomes the process owner,

24
00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:27.910
one name for the process and for the number that shows whether it works.

25
00:01:28.892 --> 00:01:31.307
For adoption and handover we often use a

26
00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:34.152
communication plan and a handover checklist.

27
00:01:35.485 --> 00:01:37.261
The third topic is Sustaining.

28
00:01:37.957 --> 00:01:40.476
Does it last, even when the project is gone?

29
00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:43.116
Expect the three-month dip.

30
00:01:43.878 --> 00:01:47.466
Once the project is gone, attention goes to something else.

31
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.885
Short, regular checks keep it alive.

32
00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:55.652
Every month the owner looks at the trend with the team, not at one week.

33
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.397
Agree a follow-up and a trigger in advance.

34
00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:03.265
If the number drops too far, the owner calls us.

35
00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:08.909
For sustaining we often use a layered process audit and a KPI board.

36
00:02:10.224 --> 00:02:13.010
The fourth topic is Benefits and reflection.

37
00:02:13.704 --> 00:02:15.341
Did it deliver what we promised?

38
00:02:16.408 --> 00:02:19.102
The instruction and the training are the output.

39
00:02:19.871 --> 00:02:22.205
People working differently is the outcome.

40
00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:25.369
The benefit is the measurable gain.

41
00:02:26.082 --> 00:02:31.364
The rent of the old hall stops, and line 3 stays as fast as at the baseline.

42
00:02:32.353 --> 00:02:36.126
A benefit owner in the line makes sure the benefit comes in.

43
00:02:36.872 --> 00:02:41.132
That is the sponsor, not the consultant, because the consultant will be gone.

44
00:02:42.115 --> 00:02:47.850
For benefits and reflection we often use an A3 report and an after-action review.

45
00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.311
It all connects.

46
00:02:51.006 --> 00:02:55.836
First the standard, then the line that takes it over, then the checks that hold it.

47
00:02:56.552 --> 00:02:58.944
The benefits show whether it was worth it.

48
00:03:00.016 --> 00:03:04.580
Line 4 comes later, and then we take along what line 3 taught us.

49
00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:07.543
This is the map of Projects.

50
00:03:08.266 --> 00:03:11.424
Land is the sixth station on the road of a project.

51
00:03:12.509 --> 00:03:15.226
Land has four topics, each with four levels.

52
00:03:16.283 --> 00:03:19.928
Start with Standardised work and training, at Basics level.

53
00:03:20.939 --> 00:03:25.351
At Working knowledge you learn standardised work and working with resistance.

54
00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:29.592
Then come leader standard work and hard and soft savings.

55
00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:33.622
At Advanced it is about skills and communication.

56
00:03:34.386 --> 00:03:36.743
Then come tiered meetings and reflection.

57
00:03:37.755 --> 00:03:41.551
At Expert you keep the standard alive and hand over to the line.

58
00:03:42.277 --> 00:03:45.226
Then come audits and rolling out to other lines.

59
00:03:46.244 --> 00:03:50.400
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
